  "description": "This EEG dataset comprises electrophysiological recordings from 62 obese and non-obese preteens performing a delayed-verification arithmetic task. The study investigates the effect of obesity on neural correlates of math processing in children with varying mathematical abilities using event-related potentials. Data were acquired using a 128-channel Geodesic Hydrocell Sensor Net system.",
  "methods_description": "EEG data were acquired using a Geodesic Net Amps 300 system with 128-channel Geodesic Hydrocell Sensor Net (Magstim EGI, Eugene OR, USA) running Netstation 4.5.2 software. Stimuli were designed and administered using E-Prime software (Version 2) at the Arkansas Children Nutrition Center. Participant data include age, gender, body mass index (BMI), and task performance.",
